    "kind": "definition_of_done",
    "summary": "- The `Tally-Signature` header is now `t=\u003cunix\u003e,v1=\u003chex\u003e[,v1=\u003chex\u003e]`, each v1 signed over `\"\u003ct\u003e.\u003cbody\u003e\"`. The previous secret also signs for 24 hours after `POST /v1/webhook-endpoints/{id}/rotate-secret`. `webhooks.SignatureHeader` and `webhooks.Verify` are added with the specified behaviour and errors, and `webhooks.Sign` keeps its meaning.\n- Unit tests cover Verify (tolerance edges, header parsing, error order) and secret overlap across rotations. An API test covers the rotate endpoint.\n- `go build ./...`, `go test ./...` and `go vet ./...` pass.",
